# Copy to migration.env and fill in. Sourced by lib.sh (which every phase script sources).
#
# TENANT, ACCOUNT, HOSTED_ZONE_ID, and ECR_ACCOUNT are required up front — the scripts fail
# fast with a clear error if any of them is missing, since none of them has a safe generic
# default (they're specific to YOUR tenant/account). OIDC_ID is filled in for you by
# 01-capture-identity.sh once you run it.

TENANT=<YOUR_TENANT_NAME>            # your (legacy) tenant's short name, e.g. the name used in its cluster/namespace
ENV=dev                              # dev | qa | preview | prod — ask your Promethium contact which applies to you
ACCOUNT=<YOUR_AWS_ACCOUNT_ID>        # AWS account id that hosts your tenant's EKS cluster
REGION=<YOUR_REGION>                 # AWS region of your tenant's EKS cluster, e.g. us-east-1
NAMESPACE=intelligentedge            # namespace the tenant runs in (standard; change only if yours differs)

# Route53 hosted zone id that serves <ENV>.promethium.ai for your tenant. Ask your
# Promethium contact if you don't have this handy.
HOSTED_ZONE_ID=<YOUR_ROUTE53_ZONE_ID>

# The Promethium container-registry AWS account (used only to build the ECR ARNs the
# ECR-pull IAM role needs in 02-prereq.sh) — this is NOT your own AWS account above.
# Provided by your Promethium contact.
ECR_ACCOUNT=<PROMETHIUM_REGISTRY_ACCOUNT — provided by your Promethium contact>

# Filled by 01-capture-identity.sh (the tenant cluster's IAM OIDC provider id):
OIDC_ID=

# Optional overrides (defaults are derived in lib.sh from TENANT/ENV/ACCOUNT/REGION above —
# leave these blank/commented unless your cluster or context naming is non-standard):
# CLUSTER=promethium-datafabric-<ENV>-<TENANT>-eks-cluster
# SPOKE_CTX=arn:aws:eks:<REGION>:<ACCOUNT>:cluster/<CLUSTER>
# HUB_CTX=                           # operator-only (Promethium's own hub context) — customers leave this unset

# 05-wipe.sh mantra carve-out. Leave blank to AUTO-DETECT (spares the live mantra-edge layer
# when a mantra-edge* deployment is present in the namespace). Set true to force-keep it, or
# false to force the plain wipe (delete everything). Non-mantra tenants: leave blank.
# MANTRA_TENANT=
